/*
 * What Configure.app shows for this driver.
 *
 * IT IS "Long Name" THAT REACHES THE SCREEN.  The version was put in the
 * key above first, on the reasoning that Configure looks a driver up by its
 * Server Name; the operator then reported the panel reading
 *   "OpenStep MGA G450 replacement display driver, wit"
 * -- 49 characters of a 73-character "Long Name", cut mid-word.  So that is
 * the string that shows, and it was too long to reach its own version.
 *
 * KEEP IT SHORT.  49 characters got through once, but the field is AppKit
 * text in a proportional font, so what fits is a WIDTH and not a count --
 * a wider string would be cut sooner.  32 characters leaves room to be
 * wrong about that.  pkg/verify-driver-pkg.sh holds both strings to a
 * budget so this cannot come back.
 *
 * AND THE VERSION IS NOT IN HERE.  It was, briefly, and the operator then
 * saw the panel show "v1.1" and "v0.5" side by side -- because Configure
 * ALREADY has a version field, fed by "Version" in Default.table, and that
 * had sat at a development 0.5 since before 1.0.  Two numbers on one panel
 * is worse than the truncation it was meant to fix.  The version lives in
 * the field built for it; this string is a name.
 */
"OSMGADisplay" = "OpenStep MGA G450 Display";
"Long Name" = "OpenStep MGA G450 Display";
